<title>GREECE: GREEK JAN REVISED CPI INFLATION DROPS TO 6.8PCT Y/Y.</title>
<headline>GREEK JAN REVISED CPI INFLATION DROPS TO 6.8PCT Y/Y.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's revised CPI inflation fell to 6.8 percent year-on-year in January from 8.4 percent in January 1996 and 10.7 percent in January 1995, the National Statistics Service (NSS) said in a statement.  </p>
<p>Average revised CPI inflation fell to 8.1 percent in the period January 97- February 96 compared to 8.8 percent in the same 12-month period a year ago, it said.  </p>
<p> Consumer Price Index   January 97  December 96   January 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month	    -0.5%	  0.0%	  -0.5</p>
<p> Year-on-year		 6.8%	  7.3%	   8.4%</p>
<p> Index (1994=100)	   121.2	 121.8	  113.6</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
